{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/127164-you-missed-two","id":127164,"title":"You missed two.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-06T19:11:02-07:00","id":127164,"title":"You missed two.","content":"After reading the first chapter, I went back to the relationships that the Unchained have with the other denizens of the World of Darkness. I notice that there were two missing from the list: Mummies and Sin-Eaters. Why were they omitted? Wasn't there enough room? Are encounters with these two races so poor that they aren't even mentioning?<br /> <br /> What are the relationships that Demons have with the Bound and the Arisen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T19:55:49-07:00","id":127188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/127164-you-missed-two#post127164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the first chapter, I went back to the relationships that the Unchained have with the other denizens of the World of Darkness. I notice that there were two missing from the list: Mummies and Sin-Eaters. Why were they omitted? Wasn't there enough room? Are encounters with these two races so poor that they aren't even mentioning?<br /> <br /> What are the relationships that Demons have with the Bound and the Arisen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stereotypes sections of the Guardians and the Tempters, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T06:50:04-07:00","id":127435,"title":"","content":"In answer to your first question, as the person who wrote that section I can tell you it was because those were the two cores to which I didn't have ready access when I was working on it. Mummy was brand new, and Sin Eaters had slipped under my radar. Rather than guess at the themes and capabilities of characters from games I hadn't read (and probably get it wrong in ways that would annoy fans of those games), I made the conscious decision to leave them out. It was really as prosaic as that.<br /> <br /> I have since read Mummy and can think of some interesting ways the two could intersect. Saboteurs might &quot;guide the lightning&quot; by leading an Arisen into the middle of one of the God-Machine's projects, for example, or maybe the God-Machine is familiar enough with the Sothic cycle to build Infrastructure that takes advantage of the sudden appearance of a deathless avatar of nearly forgotten gods. Like the qashmallim, the Arisen are powerful servants of Something Else with agendas the Unchained don't understand. Sure, demons might find clever ways to place them on a collision course with their enemies, but most of the time it's probably a better idea to just stay out of the way of the single-minded juggarnaut that is carving a path of destruction to...whatever goal it has in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:56:27-07:00","id":127554,"title":"","content":"So Sin-Eaters and Mummies don't get a GENERAL concession, but get a specific concession due to the opinion of an Incarnation and/or Agenda. Ooooooookkaayyy. :-~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T10:50:55-07:00","id":127588,"title":"","content":"Nothing <i>has</i> a general consensus beyond the big three. They might have slightly more dynamic understanding since two things look at them, but that's not saying much.<br /> <br /> And to be fair, there's a lot to look at with a very select number.<br /> <br /> EDIT:Oh, yer talking about Chapter One. That makes a lot more sense, actually.<br /> <br /> Still, space and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T14:33:50-07:00","id":127736,"title":"","content":"Seriously. No grand conspiracy. Not even really a space crunch (this time). I wasn't specifically instructed to write one for every single splat in the WoD, and I was operating on a deadline that didn't really permit me to purchase and absorb two more core books, so I made a conscious decision not to write about those splats about which I knew next to nothing.<br /> <br /> I meant no insult to those games or to their fans. I just remember too many cWOD books where people writing for Game X would describe relationships between Xs and Ys that showed little to no familiarity with Game Y. I didn't want to be that guy, you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T15:24:39-07:00","id":127770,"title":"","content":"If I were an Inquisitor, I'd be extremely intrigued about how similar the Arisen are to Angels of the God-Machine. *puts on demon-horned tin-foil hat* Maybe the Arisen were an early attempt to turn mortals into Angels. Maybe Angels are the result of a perfected Rite of Return, a rite that bears remarkable similarity to the Occult Matrices of the God-Machine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T16:47:51-07:00","id":127826,"title":"","content":"Looking back on this, I could see that the other Agendas would think more on Sin-Eaters, since they are well-known by both the Psychopomp Incarnation and the Temptor Agenda, meaning that more Unchained could corroborate with said Incarnation and Agenda. Being that the Guardian Incarnation seems to be the only ones to mention the Arisen, that makes me think that the others would believe that Mummies are just a Glitch that all Guardians experience during their Fall and nothing more, though that's my opinion given the info at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T16:50:40-07:00","id":127830,"title":"","content":"Also a thought that Demons would have, if they meet an Arisen, either as their own entity or as a Cover they weaseled out of a cultist of said Arisen, is that Irem was a project of the God Machine that reached fruition when the Nameless Empire vanished long ago, and the Arisen are trying to resurrect the project as if it shouldn't have ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T17:01:37-07:00","id":127834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JackalopeVegas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/127164-you-missed-two?p=127826#post127826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking back on this, I could see that the other Agendas would think more on Sin-Eaters, since they are well-known by both the Psychopomp Incarnation and the Temptor Agenda, meaning that more Unchained could corroborate with said Incarnation and Agenda. Being that the Guardian Incarnation seems to be the only ones to mention the Arisen, that makes me think that the others would believe that Mummies are just a Glitch that all Guardians experience during their Fall and nothing more, though that's my opinion given the info at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a baffling and faintly ridiculous interpretation to make when the far simpler explanation is &quot;the Stereotypes section has room for the other X/Y-splats, the Big Three, and Mortals, and while Demon pushed that space constraint a bit further than usual it still only has room for one extra stereotype per splat.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, lest it need reminding: we're talking about secretive and metaphysically distinct supernatural groupings. <i>None of them</i> are &quot;well-known&quot; to the average member of the other groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}